;; compiler/fibref/heap.fib: the audited heap, the memory audit (docs/design/fibref-port.md section 4). OWNER: package F1.
;; Port of crates/fibref/src/heap/ at seed-1 (2,122 lines), and the rules new since (steal, take, put, peek, move-in, ROOMY arrays, in-place array
;; primitives). A facade: the parts live in compiler/fibref/heap/ (types, state, store, cascade, shared, access, life, unique, immortal, audit, scc, text,
;; inplace). The heap is a value of cells passed as one argument (no global state). An operation validates before it changes anything: after an `Err`
;; the heap is as it was. Object ids are indices into the table and are never reused.
(ns fibref.heap
  (:export-from fibref.heap.types fibref.heap.life fibref.heap.access fibref.heap.unique fibref.heap.shared fibref.heap.immortal
                fibref.heap.audit fibref.heap.text fibref.heap.inplace))
